    "body": "<!-- Thank you for your contribution! Please follow these guidelines to enhance your pull request. If anything is unclear, submit your PR and reach out to maintainers for assistance. Join our Slack community at https://slack.sglang.io to discuss further. -->\r\n\r\n<!-- PR title: [Type] scope: title, or [Type] [Hardware] scope: title.\r\nType: Feat, Fix, Refactor, Perf, Doc, Test, CI, or Chore.\r\nScope: any module or model name (no fixed list or letter-case restriction), e.g. attention, qwen3, or flash-attn.\r\nHardware: optional single tag without spaces. Use uppercase hardware tags (AMD, NVIDIA, NPU, MI300X), except for exactly these four spellings: Intel, Apple, Huawei, Ascend.\r\nTitle: no letter-case restriction.\r\nReverts: use GitHub's default title, Revert \"original title\".\r\nExamples: [Fix] attention: Fix KV cache indexing; [Perf] [AMD] flash-attn: Optimize decode performance. -->\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nWith a negative prompt, FLUX.2-dev runs the negative (CFG) branch without RoPE position info, because `Flux2PipelineConfig.prepare_neg_cond_kwargs` returns `{}`.\r\nThis makes images over-saturated, and with `--enable-cfg-parallel` + torch.compile on torch 2.12 the two GPUs compile different graphs and the run hangs (SPMD check). \r\nThis PR builds `freqs_cis` (rope) for the negative prompt the same way as for the positive prompt, as `Flux2KleinBasePipelineConfig` already does.\r\nhttps://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/17e94c4677d7beb58a89b104fd61b3768994e45e/python/sglang/multimodal_gen/configs/pipeline_configs/flux.py#L883-L900\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nbuilds `freqs_cis` for the negative prompt the same way as for the positive prompt, as `Flux2KleinBasePipelineConfig` already does.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n```\r\nexport HIP_FORCE_DEV_KERNARG=0\r\nexport SGLANG_DIFFUSION_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=rocm\r\nexport ENABLE_CK=0\r\nMODEL=\"/mnt/raid/models/FLUX.2-dev/\"\r\n\r\nPROMPT=\"A cat and a dog baking a cake together in a kitchen. \\\r\nThe cat is carefully measuring flour, while the dog is stirring the batter with a wooden spoon. \\\r\nThe kitchen is cozy, with sunlight streaming through the window.\"\r\n\r\nHIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 \\\r\nsglang generate \\\r\n  --model-path \"${MODEL}\" \\\r\n  --log-level info \\\r\n  --prompt \"${PROMPT}\" \\\r\n  --negative-prompt \"blurry, low quality, watermark, text\" \\\r\n  --720p \\\r\n  --num-inference-steps 50 \\\r\n  --seed 42 \\\r\n  --save-output \\\r\n  --num-gpus 2 \\\r\n  --enable-cfg-parallel \\\r\n  --dit-layerwise-offload false \\\r\n  --dit-cpu-offload false \\\r\n  --vae-cpu-offload false \\\r\n  --text-encoder-cpu-offload false \\\r\n  --enable-torch-compile true \\\r\n  --offload-during-compile false \\\r\n  --warmup-mode request\r\n```\r\nBefore:\r\n<img width=\"986\" height=\"554\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f82c2701-518c-47ef-a9b7-bbe882be9b41\" />\r\nAfter:\r\n<img width=\"986\" height=\"554\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e602b5d8-97d4-4cf4-b9c1-3dd2876e9d2a\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\nFLUX.2-dev, 1280x720, 50 steps, seed 42, 2x MI455X, `--enable-cfg-parallel --enable-torch-compile true --warmup-mode request`, image `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.23-rocm10-mi45x-20261030` (torch 2.11). Numbers are from the sglang log of the warmed-up request.\r\n\r\n| Stage | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| TextEncodingStage | 0.0031 s | 0.0030 s |\r\n| DenoisingStage | 16.9486 s | 16.5543 s |\r\n| Denoising avg time per step | 0.2294 s | 0.2223 s |\r\n| DecodingStage | 0.0041 s | 0.0040 s |\r\n| Warmed-up request (E2E) | 16.97 s | 16.57 s |\r\n| Peak memory | 110332 MB | 110332 MB |\r\n\r\nOn `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.23-rocm101-mi45x-20261030` (torch 2.12), the same command hangs during torch.compile warmup before this PR. After it: TextEncodingStage 0.0030 s, DenoisingStage 16.5354 s (0.2273 s/step), DecodingStage 0.0046 s, E2E 16.55 s.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41494640214](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41494640214)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41494640295](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41494640295)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41494640281](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41494640281)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n\r\n> [!TIP]\r\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\r\n>\r\n> ```text\r\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\r\n> ```\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
